&lt;p&gt;Are you looking to own the customer-facing experience for JetBrains products, from how individuals and organizations buy and manage software to how licensing and entitlements work behind the scenes?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About JetBrains&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We create intelligent software development tools for developers and teams. More than 15 million users, over 300,000 companies, and 88 of the Fortune Global Top 100 rely on our products to solve real, complex problems. Our mission is simple: make development teams more productive and AI adoptable at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll lead the strategy for BAD (Business Application Development) Product. You’ll tackle the complex web of purchases, subscriptions, organization administration, and usage-based services, making sure our customers have a smooth, coherent experience every step of the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work closely with engineering, design, analytics, QA, and BAD Platform, as well as Sales, Customer Success, and Finance teams. You’ll have the autonomy to drive product discovery, validate hypotheses through data and experimentation, and define the long-term vision for our licensing and administration ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day to day, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the product vision, strategy, and roadmap for BAD Product systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uncover user friction through customer research, support data, telemetry, and feedback from internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map and improve end-to-end customer journeys covering purchasing, subscriptions, licensing, and administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps, overlaps, and inconsistencies across sub-systems to build a clear, unified user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering, design, analytics, and QA from early discovery through launch and continuous iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track key product metrics for adoption, conversion, and support demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate product direction, trade-offs, and progress clearly to cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ownership mindset, taking responsibility for outcomes, not just task completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear focus on underlying problems and desired outcomes rather than immediate feature requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with technical complexity, trade-offs, and systems thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A preference for quality, long-term sustainability, and user trust over short-term fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to make grounded decisions using customer research, analytics, and experimentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills across multi-disciplinary teams and distinct business areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of managing technically complex SaaS, enterprise, or B2B product areas end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience driving product discovery, user research, and roadmap prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating complex customer journeys, multi-team dependencies, and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience making data-informed decisions using telemetry, product metrics, and experimentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work comfortably alongside engineering teams on technical details, APIs, data models, and system integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In practice, success means building a licensing and administration experience that feels seamless to the user and resilient under the hood. You&#39;ll bring clarity to ambiguous systems, simplify fragmented customer flows, and establish reliable product metrics. Ultimately, you succeed by removing friction for millions of developers and admins, allowing them to focus on their actual work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join JetBrains?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong base salary – We offer competitive pay that reflects your skills and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work schedule – Enjoy the freedom to work from home or from the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra time off – More days to relax, recharge, and do the things you love.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development opportunities – Access to conferences, courses, and language classes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation support – Assistance to help make your move as smooth and stress-free as possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free meals and snacks – Lunch and refreshments provided to keep you fueled.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health and wellness – On-site gyms or sports club stipends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal events – Company-wide celebrations and team gatherings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer. We know great ideas can come from anyone, anywhere. That’s why we do our best to create an open and inclusive workplace – one that welcomes everyone regardless of their background, identity, religion, age, accessibility needs, or orientation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds like you, we’d love to read your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Some benefits may vary depending on location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(254, 254, 254);&quot;&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We know great ideas can come from anyone, anywhere. That’s why we do our best to create an open and inclusive workplace – one that welcomes everyone regardless of their background, identity, religion, age, accessibility needs, or orientation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;We process the data provided in your job application in accordance with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jetbrains.com/legal/docs/privacy/privacy-recruitment/&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notre équipe Decathlon App recherche un·e Staff Product Manager (f/m/d) en CDI basé·e à Lille ou Paris.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au cœur de l&#39;écosystème digital de Decathlon, l&#39;équipe &lt;strong&gt;Decathlon App&lt;/strong&gt; fait le pont entre nos expériences e-commerce et le commerce physique. Notre mission dépasse la simple transaction : nous construisons un compagnon sportif quotidien, personnalisé et enrichi pour accompagner des millions d&#39;utilisateur·ices dans leur pratique. Rejoindre notre équipe produit globale (iOS &amp;amp; Android), c&#39;est évoluer dans un environnement stimulant où l&#39;autonomie, l&#39;impact à grande échelle et l&#39;excellence méthodologique sont au cœur de nos défis quotidiens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TA FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant que Staff Product Manager (f/m/d), tu apporteras la vision stratégique et l&#39;architecture fonctionnelle nécessaires pour faire passer notre application mobile à l&#39;échelle supérieure. Tu opéreras avec une grande autonomie sur des enjeux complexes pour transformer l&#39;expérience Decathlon App et garantir la cohérence de l&#39;écosystème.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tes responsabilités s&#39;articulent autour de 4 piliers stratégiques :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alignement stratégique, gestion des parties prenantes &amp;amp; vision app&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter la valeur globale (&lt;em&gt;macro view&lt;/em&gt;) générée par les initiatives mobiles clés sur l&#39;ensemble de l&#39;écosystème business et client, au-delà des backlogs d&#39;équipes individuelles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Porter la vision produit auprès de la direction exécutive, des leaders business et des parties prenantes transversales pour aligner l&#39;organisation sur la roadmap de l&#39;application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Définir les orientations stratégiques sur les segments utilisateurs prioritaires sur les points de contact mobiles natifs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Suivre et optimiser les métriques de performance macro tout au long du funnel : notoriété, trafic, conversion, rétention et taux de réachat.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture fonctionnelle &amp;amp; orchestration End-to-End&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agir en tant qu&#39;Architecte Fonctionnel·le principal·e en définissant la répartition des périmètres entre les squads afin d&#39;éliminer les frictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travailler en triade étroite avec les Staff Tech/Principal Engineers et les Staff UX Designers pour aligner l&#39;architecture technique, les systèmes de design et la vision produit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concevoir des parcours omnicanaux sans couture reliant la découverte mobile, les interactions en magasin (ex: Scan &amp;amp; Go, retrait), le paiement et les services sportifs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sparring stratégique &amp;amp; de-risking produit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conseiller et accompagner les Group Product Managers (GPM) et Product Managers (PM) face aux dépendances complexes de l&#39;application et aux pièges classiques du produit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structurer des stratégies de réduction des risques (&lt;em&gt;de-risking&lt;/em&gt;) sur les projets majeurs pour identifier au plus tôt les enjeux d&#39;appétence, de viabilité et d&#39;utilisabilité.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mener des boucles de validation concrètes (A/B testing, multivariés, tests d&#39;utilisabilité de prototypes) pour valider les hypothèses avant le déploiement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Élévation de la culture &amp;amp; des pratiques produit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accompagner la communauté PM vers les meilleures pratiques produit modernes (frameworks de discovery, expérimentation continue, Opportunity Solution Trees - OST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promouvoir l&#39;adoption des possibilités liées à l&#39;IA et des méthodologies avancées pour enrichir l&#39;expérience utilisateur et l&#39;efficacité des squads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Jouer un rôle de multiplicateur d&#39;impact pour faire grandir la communauté Produit, sans agir en tant que manager hiérarchique.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CE QUE TU APPORTES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérience Mobile Native&lt;/strong&gt; : Solide parcours (7 ans+) en gestion de produits avec une expérience terrain dans la mise à l&#39;échelle d&#39;applications mobiles natives (iOS &amp;amp; Android) dans des environnements digitaux à fort volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complexité E-commerce &amp;amp; Retail&lt;/strong&gt; : Solide expérience dans l&#39;e-commerce, les plateformes digitales ou le retail omnicanal où les produits digitaux se connectent directement aux points de contact opérationnels physiques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impact transversal&lt;/strong&gt; : Expérience démontrée dans l&#39;alignement inter-équipes et les initiatives architecturales au sein d&#39;organisations produit multi-équipes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stratégie d&#39;Application Native&lt;/strong&gt; : Compréhension approfondie des paradigmes de design iOS/Android, des mécaniques des app stores, de l&#39;analytics mobile et des stratégies d&#39;engagement via push.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery &amp;amp; Analytics&lt;/strong&gt; : Expertise des méthodes de discovery quantitatives et qualitatives, de l&#39;A/B testing, de l&#39;optimisation de conversion (CRO) et des Opportunity Solution Trees (OST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture fonctionnelle&lt;/strong&gt; : Capacité à structurer des problèmes business complexes en stratégies de MVP/V0/V1 claires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication exécutive&lt;/strong&gt; : Aisance pour traduire des architectures produit, des métriques UX et des données en présentations claires et convaincantes pour les dirigeants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IA &amp;amp; Outils modernes&lt;/strong&gt; : Curiosité et expérience pratique de l&#39;intégration de l&#39;IA dans les workflows produit et les expériences utilisateurs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posture &amp;amp; Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence stratégique et intelligence émotionnelle (leadership sans autorité hiérarchique).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à s&#39;épanouir dans l&#39;ambiguïté et à structurer des défis complexes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Esprit de collaboration fort en Triade (Tech, Design, UXR, Data, Business).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathie et volonté de transmettre aux PM plus juniors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CE QUE NOUS T’OFFRONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organisation de travail hybride ;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Matériel fourni en accord avec tes missions et nos engagements sociétaux (Mac ou Windows) ;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une équipe de projet locale au sein d&#39;un réseau mondial (possibilité de carrière internationale) ;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Développement des compétences et accompagnement (diversité des projets, formations internes et externes, etc.) ;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Package de rémunération (actionnariat salarié, bonus mensuels/trimestriels).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTRE ENGAGEMENT EN FAVEUR DE L&#39;INCLUSION ET DE L&#39;ACCESSIBILITE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez Decathlon, nous reconnaissons l&#39;immense valeur qu&#39;apporte la diversité à nos équipes et nous nous efforçons continuellement de favoriser et de cultiver un lieu de travail inclusif et équitable : c&#39;est pourquoi l&#39;Inclusion est l&#39;un de nos Fondamentaux Humains. Nous encourageons les personnes de tous horizons et de toutes capacités à postuler, car nous sommes convaincu·es que la diversité des pensées, des cultures, des identités et des expériences vécues nous rend plus fort·es. Decathlon s&#39;engage également à offrir un processus de sélection inclusif et accessible à tous les candidat·es. En cas de besoin d&#39;aménagement, tu peux en faire la demande via le formulaire de candidature, celle-ci sera confidentielle. Ces demandes n&#39;affectent pas le résultat du processus de recrutement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🇬🇧 ENGLISH VERSION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Decathlon App team is looking for a Staff Product Manager (f/m/d) on a Permanent Contract (CDI) based in Lille or Paris.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the core of Decathlon&#39;s digital ecosystem, the &lt;strong&gt;Decathlon App&lt;/strong&gt; team acts as the ultimate bridge between our digital commerce and physical store experiences. Our mission goes beyond transactions: we are building an indispensable daily sports companion for millions of users. Joining our global mobile team (iOS &amp;amp; Android) means evolving in a high-impact environment where autonomy, scaling challenges, and product excellence drive everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Manager (f/m/d), you will provide the strategic direction and functional architecture needed to scale our mobile platform across multiple product teams. Operating with high autonomy, you will address complex challenges to shape our long-term app experience and guarantee ecosystem cohesion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission centers on 4 strategic pillars:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Alignment, Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; App Vision&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the holistic value (&lt;em&gt;macro view&lt;/em&gt;) generated by key mobile initiatives across the business and customer ecosystem, moving beyond individual squad backlogs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver high-impact narratives and presentations to executive leadership, business directors, and cross-functional stakeholders to align the organization on major platform shifts and app roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set strategic direction for key user segments across native mobile touchpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and optimize macro success metrics across the entire journey: Awareness, Traffic, Conversion, Retention, and Repeat Purchase Rate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Functional Architecture &amp;amp; End-to-End Orchestration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the lead Functional Architect, defining how functional scope and boundaries are distributed across app feature squads to eliminate overlap and friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in tight Triad Collaboration with Staff/Principal Engineers and Staff UX Designers to align technical architecture, mobile design systems, and product vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design seamless, connected user journeys linking mobile discovery, in-store interactions (e.g., Scan &amp;amp; Go, store pickup), checkout, and sports services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Sparring &amp;amp; Product De-Risking&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted strategic advisor and sparring partner for Group Product Managers (GPMs) and PMs to help them navigate complex app dependencies and product traps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formulate and drive product de-risking strategies for high-stakes app initiatives, identifying desirability, viability, and usability risks early in discovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run concrete validation loops (A/B tests, multivariate testing, prototype usability tests) to validate hypotheses before engineering deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elevating Product Craft &amp;amp; Mastery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upskill the PM community on modern product practices, standardizing discovery frameworks, continuous experimentation, and Opportunity Solution Trees (OST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive organizational adoption of AI-first possibilities and advanced product methodologies to amplify app experience and squad efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a force multiplier: elevate the collective bar of the product management community without operating as a formal people manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO THE TABLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mobile Native Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;: Proven track record (7+ years) in Product Management with deep hands-on experience scaling native mobile applications (iOS &amp;amp; Android) in high-scale digital environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;E-Commerce &amp;amp; Retail Complexity&lt;/strong&gt;: Solid background in e-commerce, digital platforms, or omnichannel retail where digital products connect directly with physical operational touchpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transverse Scale&lt;/strong&gt;: Demonstrated experience driving cross-squad alignment and architectural initiatives across multi-team product organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Native App Product Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;: Deep understanding of iOS/Android design paradigms, app store mechanics, mobile analytics, and push engagement strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Discovery &amp;amp; De-Risking&lt;/strong&gt;: Expertise in quantitative and qualitative discovery methods, CRO, A/B testing frameworks, and Opportunity Solution Trees (OST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Functional Architecture &amp;amp; Scoping&lt;/strong&gt;: Ability to structure complex business problems into clear MVP/V0/V1 scoping playbooks and boundary maps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Communication &amp;amp; Storytelling&lt;/strong&gt;: Ability to translate complex product architectures, UX metrics, and data insights into clear, persuasive executive presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; Modern Product Stack&lt;/strong&gt;: Curiosity and practical experience integrating AI capabilities into product workflows and user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills &amp;amp; Behaviors:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Influence &amp;amp; Emotional Intelligence (influencing without hierarchical authority).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thriving in Ambiguity (highly autonomous self-starter).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triad &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Collaboration (Staff Tech, Staff Design, UXR, Data, Business).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth Mindset &amp;amp; Empathy (humble approach and dedicating time to mentor).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER YOU&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work organization;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equipment provided tailored to your role and our sustainability commitments (Mac or Windows);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Local project team within a global network (international career opportunities);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous skills development and support (diverse projects, internal and external training, etc.);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive compensation package (employee stock ownership, monthly/quarterly bonuses).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUR COMMITMENT TO INCLUSION AND ACCESSIBILITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Decathlon, we recognize the immense value that diversity brings to our teams, and we continuously strive to foster and cultivate an inclusive and equitable workplace: this is why Inclusion is one of our Human Fundamentals. We encourage people of all backgrounds and abilities to apply, as we are convinced that diversity of thought, culture, identity, and lived experience makes us stronger. Decathlon is also committed to offering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process for all candidates. If you require any reasonable accommodations during the process, you can request them via the application form, and your request will remain confidential. These requests will not affect the outcome of your hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Imaginez si la technologie nous permettait de repousser les frontières et d&#39;offrir des expériences sportives inédites. C&#39;est précisément notre ambition chez Decathlon Digital ! Nous sommes une équipe de plus de 5 000 experts en ingénierie logicielle, gestion de produits, données, cloud et cybersécurité, répartis à Paris, Lille et Amsterdam. Ensemble, nous créons la plus vaste plateforme sportive numérique, en exploitant les innovations technologiques pour optimiser la chaîne de valeur, concevoir des expériences connectées et donner une seconde vie à nos produits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changeons la donne pour de bon.&lt;/strong&gt; Notre passion du sport nous guide et nous voulons qu’elle perdure. C’est pourquoi nous nous engageons à bâtir un modèle technologique plus durable, en réduisant notre impact direct sur l&#39;environnement, et en créant un espace sûr et inclusif pour apprendre et nous épanouir ensemble. Rejoins l’équipe et façonnons le futur du sport.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At &lt;strong&gt;Sofico&lt;/strong&gt;, we’re shaping the future of mobility – and we’re doing it together. Our software, &lt;strong&gt;Miles&lt;/strong&gt;, enables companies worldwide to manage their leasing, fleet and mobility operations in one integrated platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From our &lt;strong&gt;Macquarie Park&lt;/strong&gt; office, we’re looking for an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Senior Project Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to lead complex, high-impact software implementation projects for our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior, customer-facing role where you’ll take ownership of projects from planning through implementation, go-live and transition to support. You’ll shape the project approach, lead cross-functional teams, work closely with senior customer stakeholders and maintain oversight of scope, budget, quality and risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex &lt;strong&gt;end-to-end ERP and software implementation projects&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring successful delivery against scope, timeline, budget and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and shape the project approach best suited to the customer and project while aligning with Sofico’s implementation methodology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish project plans, governance, milestones, responsibilities and communication structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with &lt;strong&gt;senior customer stakeholders&lt;/strong&gt; and represent Sofico in Steering Committees and key project meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional project teams and coordinate multiple workstreams, resources, dependencies and priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively manage project risks, issues and change, taking corrective action where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong commercial oversight, including project budgets, invoicing and input into revenue forecasting and recognition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead projects through go-live, hypercare, customer acceptance and transition to support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your skills and interests:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re an experienced Project Manager who enjoys leading complex &lt;strong&gt;implementations while remaining close to the delivery. You combine strong project management capability with strategic thinking, commercial awareness and confident stakeholder management.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Significant experience managing ERP, enterprise software or complex IT implementation projects.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience delivering projects end-to-end, from mobilisation and planning through implementation and go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership, negotiation and senior stakeholder management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing multiple workstreams, priorities and project dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of project planning, governance, risk and change management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial awareness with experience managing project budgets, scope and financial performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to navigate complexity, exercise sound judgement and drive practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading, mentoring and developing project teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and conflict-resolution skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within &lt;strong&gt;leasing, automotive, fleet, finance or mobility&lt;/strong&gt; would be highly regarded.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;To be eligible, you must be an Australian Citizen, Permanent Resident, or have your own pathway to PR. Unfortunately, we are unable to offer visa sponsorship for this role.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sofico, you’ll join an international, multicultural company with over 30 years of success. We double in size every five years, staying true to our open and collaborative culture even as we grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe you should be in control of your own career. That’s why we put your personal development first. With an extensive onboarding program, you’ll spend six months learning our products and getting to know the organisation with the support of a dedicated job coach. Your learning doesn’t stop there; we’ll continue to offer opportunities for growth and development throughout your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work in a modern, accessible office with flexible and hybrid work options that allow you to balance work and life. In addition, we offer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous opportunities for learning and professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onsite parking, EV charging and walking distance from the metro.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and flexible office hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Novated leasing options and mobile phone reimbursement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complimentary coffee, soft drinks, breakfast and fruit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work from home two days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team events including after-work drinks, BBQs, family days and company weekends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2 class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Company Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ecosio is a fast-growing, innovative service company and a leading provider of B2B integration, specialising in electronic data interchange (EDI), Web EDI and e-invoicing. ecosio is part of Vertex, Inc., a leading global provider of indirect tax solutions listed on Nasdaq (VERX).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our brand slogan is&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Connections That Work&lt;/em&gt; as we believe strong connections are central to successful business relationships - both external and internal. At ecosio, we hire individuals from all backgrounds and are committed to creating an inclusive work environment. We are technology lovers, set the highest standards for our solutions, and put innovative ideas first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Job Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Product Owner to own our workflow platform end to end, make bold decisions and ship AI-native automation that transforms how ecosio works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll connect with the role if you enjoy:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Having the freedom and accountability to challenge existing processes, prototype quickly and drive ideas through to company-wide adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking ambiguous workflow problems from first insight to shipped solution and measurable impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritizing features and enhancements based on business impact and user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing intuitive user interfaces and experiences for internal applications with AI workflows in mind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working directly with teams to uncover high-leverage problems and turn them into clear product bets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducting user training sessions and creating interactive documentation for clear user enablement and feature adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyzing usage data to identify optimization opportunities, adoption and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating daily with UI/UX designers and engineering teams to prototype, test, and ship high-impact tooling functionality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To connect with ecosio, it is important to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–4 years of experience in product management or a related role, preferably in a SaaS environment (e.g. Project Management software, Configuration systems, Agent systems)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Native Expertise&lt;/strong&gt; - an understanding of modern AI/ML technology (e.g. LLMs, RAGs, MCPs, agentic systems and other concepts) and ability to demonstrate how you build or optimize features and workflows with AI tools in your work or side projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in a dynamic, evolving environment, embracing new priorities and challenges as opportunities to learn and grow. Curiosity, adaptability, disciplined execution and strategic communication are part of your core values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong product vision and the ability to break the the big picture into small, shippable, impactful increments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mindset focused on how users think, ensuring our products and workflow tools are intuitive, efficient, and user-friendly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with agent building, prototyping/design tools, documentation/planning tools, ticketing systems, and analytics tools (e.g. Figma, Posthog,…)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And nice to have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A technical background or education (HTL, FH, university,..)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in workflow automation, process improvement, or configuring complex transactional systems/logs (e.g., document exchange or fintech)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of EDI concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Additional Information&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By connecting with us you will experience...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our remote-first culture lets you work remotely from one of our designated countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours to suit your schedule and priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual personal development budget to invest in conferences, courses, or career coaching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office allowance to create a workspace that fits your needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular events and trips to connect, celebrate, and have fun with the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workations of up to 90 days per year within the EU, combining travel and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellbeing support, including mental health resources and employee assistance programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional country-specific benefits based on your location&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sounds like a connection that works? Then apply now and we will get in touch soon!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to build Connections That Work by fostering a diverse and inclusive team. We are committed to making everyone feel valued and empowered to contribute their unique skills, experiences and perspectives. And now we want to connect with you.&lt;/p&gt;
